<h2 id=3D"0-scope-and-the-one-thing-to-know-first">0. Scope and the one thi=
ng to know first<a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D"file:///private/var/folders=
/hj/hx1hqg8908nf89fbssd6mq5h0000gv/T/92.html#0-scope-and-the-one-thing-to-k=
now-first" title=3D"Permanent link">=EE=A0=86</a></h2>
<p><strong>haldraw performs no image analysis of its own.</strong> There is=
 no edge detection, contour tracing, colour quantisation, connected-compone=
nt labelling, OCR or line following anywhere in the app. Every perceptual j=
udgement =E2=80=94 where a box is, whether it is a rectangle or an ellipse,=
 what colour it is, what its text says, which shapes an arrow joins =E2=80=
=94 is made by the vision model in a single request and returned as JSON. T=
he app=E2=80=99s job is to (1) prepare the image, (2) ask the question prec=
isely and constrain the answer=E2=80=99s shape, (3) check the answer struct=
urally, (4) map the answer=E2=80=99s pixel coordinates onto the board, and =
(5) insert the result as ordinary haldraw rows that the user can edit.</p>
<p>Consequently, connectors are <strong>not traced</strong>. The model repo=
rts =E2=80=9Ca connector joins shape <code>s1</code> to shape <code>s3</cod=
e>, with an arrowhead at <code>s3</code>=E2=80=9D. haldraw then draws its o=
wn straight line between those two shapes using its existing auto-anchor ro=
uting (=C2=A7C.6, =C2=A7D.4). The path in the original picture =E2=80=94 be=
nds, curves, the exact points where it touched the boxes =E2=80=94 is not r=
ecovered and is not asked for.</p>
<p>Everything below is in service of that division of labour.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id=3D"1-overview">1. Overview<a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D"file:///pr=
ivate/var/folders/hj/hx1hqg8908nf89fbssd6mq5h0000gv/T/92.html#1-overview" t=
itle=3D"Permanent link">=EE=A0=86</a></h2>
<h3 id=3D"11-one-paragraph">1.1 One paragraph<a class=3D"headerlink" href=
=3D"file:///private/var/folders/hj/hx1hqg8908nf89fbssd6mq5h0000gv/T/92.html=
#11-one-paragraph" title=3D"Permanent link">=EE=A0=86</a></h3>
<p>The user selects a reference image node (or clicks the sparkle on its <s=
trong>Reference images</strong> row) and presses <strong>Vectorize=E2=80=A6=
</strong>. The renderer fetches the stored image bytes, downsamples them so=
 the long side is at most 1568 px, and sends a PNG plus the chosen model id=
 to the main process over IPC. The main process reads the Anthropic API key=
 from the macOS keychain, builds one Messages API request (image + one-line=
 instruction, a fixed system prompt, and a JSON-schema structured-output co=
nstraint), and calls the model. The reply is parsed and validated structura=
lly; an invalid reply is sent back once with the validation error appended.=
 The validated <code>{ shapes, connectors }</code> object returns to the re=
nderer, which scales every box from image pixels into the reference node=E2=
=80=99s rectangle, resolves colours, dashes low-confidence elements, estima=
tes a font size for each text, and builds node and edge rows. Those rows ar=
e inserted as one undo step onto a =E2=80=9CDraft=E2=80=9D layer directly a=
bove the image=E2=80=99s layer, grouped and selected; the ordinary dirty-fl=
ush then writes them to SQLite. A toast reports the counts, the model and t=
he token usage.</p>
