<h3 id=3D"a4-model-choice-and-settings">A.4 Model choice and settings<a cla=
ss=3D"headerlink" href=3D"file:///private/var/folders/hj/hx1hqg8908nf89fbss=
d6mq5h0000gv/T/92.html#a4-model-choice-and-settings" title=3D"Permanent lin=
k">=EE=A0=86</a></h3>
<p><code>window.haldraw.settings.get()</code> returns <code>AppSettings { v=
ectorizeModel }</code>. The main process reads it from the <code>meta</code=
> table, key <code>vectorize.model</code>, falling back to <code>DEFAULT_VE=
CTORIZE_MODEL =3D 'claude-opus-5'</code>. The Settings dialog (<strong>File=
 =E2=96=B8 Settings=E2=80=A6</strong>, <code>=E2=8C=98,</code>, or the tool=
bar gear) writes it with <code>settings.set</code>, which trims and ignores=
 empty strings.</p>
<p>The selectable models (<code>VECTORIZE_MODELS</code> in <code>shared/typ=
es.ts</code>):</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>id</th>
<th>label</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>claude-opus-5</code></td>
<td>Claude Opus 5 (default)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>claude-sonnet-5</code></td>
<td>Claude Sonnet 5</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>claude-opus-4-8</code></td>
<td>Claude Opus 4.8</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>claude-haiku-4-5</code></td>
<td>Claude Haiku 4.5</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>The id string is passed through to the API unchanged. An id the API does=
 not know produces the =E2=80=9CModel =E2=80=A6 was not found=E2=80=9D erro=
r (=C2=A7B.9); since the select offers only these four, that arises only fr=
om a hand-edited <code>meta</code> row or an id the API has retired.</p>
