<p>What the schema does <strong>not</strong> constrain, and therefore what =
<code>validateResult</code> (=C2=A7B.7) or Step C must handle:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>id</code> uniqueness and <code>from</code>/<code>to</code> referr=
ing to real ids (checked by <code>validateResult</code>)</li>
<li><code>w</code>, <code>h</code> positivity and box position relative to =
the image (checked by <code>validateResult</code>)</li>
<li>hex format of colours (handled by Step C: a non-matching string is trea=
ted as unknown)</li>
<li><code>confidence</code> range (not checked; anything <code>&lt; 0.6</co=
de> dashes, anything else does not)</li>
<li><code>text</code> line-break encoding (the model is told <code>\n</code=
>; JSON decoding yields a real newline)</li>
</ul>
<p>The division of labour: <strong>schema</strong> guarantees the shape of =
the JSON so <code>JSON.parse</code> and the type cast are safe; <strong>pro=
mpt</strong> carries the semantics; <strong>validateResult</strong> enforce=
s the referential and geometric invariants the schema language cannot expre=
ss.</p>
<h3 id=3D"b6-what-the-model-is-asked-to-perceive">B.6 What the model is ask=
ed to perceive<a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D"file:///private/var/folders/h=
j/hx1hqg8908nf89fbssd6mq5h0000gv/T/92.html#b6-what-the-model-is-asked-to-pe=
rceive" title=3D"Permanent link">=EE=A0=86</a></h3>
<p>Restating =C2=A71.5 from the model=E2=80=99s point of view, this is the =
complete perceptual task, and nothing else is asked:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight"><pre>  for every visible shape:                   =
 for every visible connector:
    kind =E2=88=88 {rect, ellipse, diamond, text}       from: shape id at o=
ne end
    bounding box x, y, w, h (image px)          to:   shape id at the other=
 end
    text (verbatim, \n line breaks, or "")      headEnd =E2=88=88 {none, ar=
row}  (head at `to`)
    fill, stroke, textColor (#rrggbb or "")     label ("" if none)
    confidence 0=E2=80=931                              confidence 0=E2=80=
=931
    id (short, unique)
</pre></div>

<p>Not asked for, and so never present in a draft: rotation, corner radius,=
 stroke width, dash pattern, font family/weight/size, text alignment, gradi=
ents, icons, images inside shapes, connector paths or waypoints, connector =
colour or width, a head at the <code>from</code> end, head styles other tha=
n the filled arrow, containment/nesting, groups, z-order intent, and any el=
ement that is a line not joining two shapes.</p>
<h3 id=3D"b7-response-handling-and-structural-validation">B.7 Response hand=
ling and structural validation<a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D"file:///priva=
te/var/folders/hj/hx1hqg8908nf89fbssd6mq5h0000gv/T/92.html#b7-response-hand=
ling-and-structural-validation" title=3D"Permanent link">=EE=A0=86</a></h3>
<p>After a successful HTTP round trip:</p>
<ol>
<li><code>usage.input_tokens</code> and <code>usage.output_tokens</code> ar=
e added to running totals (so a retried call reports the sum of both attemp=
ts).</li>
<li><code>stop_reason =3D=3D=3D 'refusal'</code> =E2=86=92 <code>VectorizeE=
rror('model')</code> =E2=80=9CThe model declined to process this image.=E2=
=80=9D</li>
<li><code>stop_reason =3D=3D=3D 'max_tokens'</code> =E2=86=92 <code>Vectori=
zeError('output')</code> =E2=80=9C=E2=80=A6ran out of output tokens=E2=80=
=A6; try a simpler image.=E2=80=9D</li>
<li>All <code>text</code> blocks in <code>message.content</code> are concat=
enated (<code>textOf</code>).</li>
<li><code>JSON.parse(text)</code>; a throw becomes the problem string <code=
>Not valid JSON: &lt;message&gt;</code>.</li>
<li><code>validateResult(parsed, req.width, req.height)</code> returns <cod=
e>null</code> or the <strong>first</strong> problem found, as a sentence th=
e model can act on.</li>
</ol>
<p><code>validateResult</code> rules, in evaluation order:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>#</th>
<th>Check</th>
<th>Problem string</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>1</td>
<td>value is an object</td>
<td><code>Output is not an object.</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>2</td>
<td><code>shapes</code> is an array</td>
<td><code>Missing "shapes" array.</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>3</td>
<td><code>connectors</code> is an array</td>
<td><code>Missing "connectors" array.</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>4</td>
<td>each shape has a non-empty string <code>id</code></td>
<td><code>Shape &lt;i&gt;: missing id.</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>5</td>
<td>ids are unique</td>
<td><code>Shape &lt;i&gt;: duplicate id "&lt;id&gt;".</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>6</td>
<td><code>kind</code> =E2=88=88 {rect, ellipse, diamond, text}</td>
<td><code>Shape &lt;id&gt;: unknown kind "&lt;kind&gt;".</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>7</td>
<td><code>x</code>, <code>y</code>, <code>w</code>, <code>h</code> are fini=
te numbers</td>
<td><code>Shape &lt;id&gt;: &lt;k&gt; must be a number.</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>8</td>
<td><code>w &gt; 0</code> and <code>h &gt; 0</code></td>
<td><code>Shape &lt;id&gt;: w and h must be positive.</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>9</td>
<td>box overlaps the image: not <code>x + w &lt; 0</code>, not <code>y + h =
&lt; 0</code>, not <code>x &gt; W</code>, not <code>y &gt; H</code></td>
<td><code>Shape &lt;id&gt;: box lies outside the image (W=C3=97H).</code></=
td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>10</td>
<td>each connector=E2=80=99s <code>from</code> is a known id</td>
<td><code>Connector &lt;i&gt;: "from" is not a shape id.</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>11</td>
<td>each connector=E2=80=99s <code>to</code> is a known id</td>
<td><code>Connector &lt;i&gt;: "to" is not a shape id.</code></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>12</td>
<td><code>from !=3D=3D to</code></td>
<td><code>Connector &lt;i&gt;: from and to are the same shape.</code></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Rule 9 is permissive on purpose: a box may hang partly off the image (co=
mmon when the model=E2=80=99s estimate of an edge-hugging element overshoot=
s) and is only rejected when it has no overlap at all. Rule 6 and the type =
half of rule 7 duplicate what the schema enforces; they matter for the test=
-seam file (=C2=A7B.10), which bypasses the API. Finiteness, positivity (ru=
le 8) and the overlap test (rule 9) are enforced nowhere else.</p>
<p>Not validated: colour strings, confidence range, <code>headEnd</code> va=
lue (schema-enforced only), <code>text</code>/<code>label</code> types (sch=
ema-enforced only), empty <code>shapes</code> (handled in the renderer: =E2=
=80=9CThe model found no shapes in this image.=E2=80=9D).</p>
<h3 id=3D"b8-the-single-retry">B.8 The single retry<a class=3D"headerlink" =
href=3D"file:///private/var/folders/hj/hx1hqg8908nf89fbssd6mq5h0000gv/T/92.=
html#b8-the-single-retry" title=3D"Permanent link">=EE=A0=86</a></h3>
