=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=
=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=
=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=
=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=
=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=
=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=
=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=98
  system prompt, schema and all other parameters unchanged
</pre></div>

<p>The image is therefore sent (and billed) twice on a retry. The <code>&lt=
;problem&gt;</code> is one of the rule strings in =C2=A7B.7 or the <code>No=
t valid JSON: &lt;message&gt;</code> form, so the model gets a single concr=
ete fix to make (=E2=80=9CConnector 3: =E2=80=9Cto=E2=80=9D is not a shape =
id.=E2=80=9D), not a list. If the second reply also fails, the error carrie=
s the problem and the first 400 characters of the reply so the user can see=
 what came back.</p>
<p>Because the output is schema-constrained, parse failures should be rare;=
 the retry mostly catches referential errors (a connector naming an id that=
 does not exist, a duplicate id) and geometric ones (zero-width box).</p>
<h3 id=3D"b9-error-taxonomy">B.9 Error taxonomy<a class=3D"headerlink" href=
