<p>Because <code>sx</code> and <code>sy</code> are computed separately, a r=
eference the user has stretched non-uniformly gets a draft stretched the sa=
me way. Rotation of the reference node is <strong>not</strong> applied (<co=
de>rotation: 0</code> on every draft node); a rotated reference gets an unr=
otated draft over its axis-aligned frame. The floor of 4 units prevents a d=
egenerate box (a reading of the code; no comment states the reason).</p>
<p>The design note=E2=80=99s regression case =E2=80=9Creference at 50 %=E2=
=80=9D is exactly this scale: <code>sent</code> equals the stored image siz=
e (if =E2=89=A4 1568 px) while <code>ref.width</code> is half of it, so <co=
de>sx =3D 0.5</code>.</p>
