<p><code>contrastingText(hex)</code> computes WCAG relative luminance (sRGB=
 linearisation, coefficients 0.2126 / 0.7152 / 0.0722) and returns <code>#0=
b0d10</code> when luminance &gt; 0.35, else <code>#ffffff</code>. The thres=
hold 0.35 sits above the 0.179 crossover at which black and white have equa=
l contrast, so mid-tone fills (the blues and greens in the screenshot board=
s) get white text. The code and the 0.9.2 commit state the value but no rat=
ionale; this reading is the document=E2=80=99s.</p>
<p><code>base</code> is <code>defaultStyleForBackground(board.background)</=
code>, which switches between a light and a dark palette by a different, ch=
eaper luminance test (<code>isColorDark</code>, Rec. 601 weights, threshold=
 128). The two functions serve different purposes and are not meant to agre=
e.</p>
<p>Note the asymmetry: an unknown <strong>fill</strong> becomes transparent=
 (so as not to hide the reference), but an unknown <strong>stroke</strong> =
becomes the board default (so the shape has a visible outline to grab).</p>
<h3 id=3D"c4-confidence-and-the-dashed-stroke">C.4 Confidence and the dashe=
d stroke<a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D"file:///private/var/folders/hj/hx1h=
qg8908nf89fbssd6mq5h0000gv/T/92.html#c4-confidence-and-the-dashed-stroke" t=
itle=3D"Permanent link">=EE=A0=86</a></h3>
<p><code>LOW_CONFIDENCE =3D 0.6</code>. For shapes other than <code>text</c=
ode>, <code>confidence &lt; 0.6</code> sets <code>style.strokeDasharray =3D=
 '6 4'</code>; for connectors it sets the same on the edge style. Each dash=
ed element increments <code>lowConfidence</code>, which the toast reports (=
=E2=80=9CN dashed (low confidence)=E2=80=9D). Low-confidence <code>text</co=
de> shapes are counted but not visually marked, because a text node has no =
stroke to dash.</p>
<p>The dash is stored as a plain style value, so the user removes it by cho=
osing <strong>Solid</strong> in the properties panel, and it survives in th=
e <code>.haldraw</code> file like any other dash.</p>
<h3 id=3D"c5-font-size-estimation">C.5 Font size estimation<a class=3D"head=
erlink" href=3D"file:///private/var/folders/hj/hx1hqg8908nf89fbssd6mq5h0000=
gv/T/92.html#c5-font-size-estimation" title=3D"Permanent link">=EE=A0=86</a=
></h3>
<p>The model reports no font size. <code>estimateFontSize(text, w, h, kind)=
</code> derives one from the box the model measured, in canvas units (the s=
ame units as <code>w</code>, <code>h</code> after C.1). Constants model an =
Inter-like face:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>constant</th>
<th>value</th>
<th>meaning</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>CHAR_W</code></td>
<td>0.55</td>
<td>average glyph advance as a multiple of font size</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>LINE_H</code></td>
<td>1.25</td>
<td>line height as a multiple of font size</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>MIN_FONT</code> / <code>MAX_FONT</code></td>
<td>8 / 48</td>
<td>clamp</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>Empty (after trimming) text =E2=86=92 16 (the default; nothing to fit). =
Otherwise, on the trimmed text <code>t</code>: <code>lines =3D t.split('\n'=
)</code>, <code>longest =3D max line length (=E2=89=A5 1)</code>; <code>tex=
t.length</code> below means <code>t.length</code>.</p>
<p><strong>Free text</strong> (<code>kind =3D=3D 'text'</code>): the box <e=
m>is</em> the text=E2=80=99s extent, so fit both dimensions and take the sm=
aller:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight"><pre>  byHeight =3D h / (lines =C3=97 LINE_H)
  byWidth  =3D w / (longest =C3=97 CHAR_W)
  f =3D min(byHeight, byWidth)
</pre></div>

<p><strong>Text inside a shape</strong>: the box is the shape, and the text=
 occupies only part of it, wrapped by the renderer. Size so the wrapped tex=
t fills a usable fraction of the area, but never wider than 90 % of the box=
 at a capped 24-character line:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight"><pre>  usable  =3D k =C3=97 w =C3=97 h        k =
=3D 0.75 rect | 0.50 ellipse | 0.40 diamond
  byArea  =3D sqrt( usable / (text.length =C3=97 CHAR_W =C3=97 LINE_H) )
  byWidth =3D (0.9 =C3=97 w) / (min(longest, 24) =C3=97 CHAR_W)
  f =3D min(byArea, byWidth)
</pre></div>

<p>Result: <code>round(clamp(f, 8, 48))</code>.</p>
<p>The <code>k</code> factors approximate how much of the bounding box an i=
nscribed text block can use: an ellipse loses its corners, a diamond more s=
o. The <code>min(longest, 24)</code> cap assumes the renderer will wrap lin=
es longer than about 24 characters, so a single long line should not force =
a tiny font. Verified values from the 0.9.1 commit:</p>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>box</th>
<th>kind</th>
<th>text</th>
<th>result</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>397 =C3=97 119</td>
<td>rect</td>
<td>36 chars</td>
<td>27 px</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>496 =C3=97 60</td>
<td>text</td>
<td>one line, 36 chars</td>
<td>25 px</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>298 =C3=97 159</td>
<td>ellipse</td>
<td>=E2=80=94</td>
<td>20 px</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p>The commit does not give line breaks. The 27 and the 20 follow when the =
longest line is at least 24 characters, which makes both width-bound (357.3=
 / 13.2 =3D 27.07); that is the ordinary case for a single wrapped label. T=
he 25 is width-bound for a 36-character line.</p>
<p>The renderer draws the label in a <code>foreignObject</code> with 8 px p=
adding, <code>lineHeight 1.3</code>, <code>pre-wrap</code> and <code>break-=
word</code> (=C2=A7D.4). The heuristic=E2=80=99s 1.25 line height and zero =
padding are slightly optimistic relative to that, so drafts run a touch lar=
ge rather than small. (An observed consequence; the code does not state it =
as a goal.)</p>
<h3 id=3D"c6-connector-construction">C.6 Connector construction<a class=3D"=
headerlink" href=3D"file:///private/var/folders/hj/hx1hqg8908nf89fbssd6mq5h=
0000gv/T/92.html#c6-connector-construction" title=3D"Permanent link">=EE=A0=
=86</a></h3>
<p>Each <code>VectorConnector</code> becomes one <code>CanvasEdge</code> ro=
w. Nothing geometric is computed here; the edge stores only <em>what it joi=
ns</em>:</p>
