<h3 id=3D"d1-resolving-the-draft-layer">D.1 Resolving the Draft layer<a cla=
ss=3D"headerlink" href=3D"file:///private/var/folders/hj/hx1hqg8908nf89fbss=
d6mq5h0000gv/T/92.html#d1-resolving-the-draft-layer" title=3D"Permanent lin=
k">=EE=A0=86</a></h3>
<p>Done in <code>vectorizeNode</code> just before insertion:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight"><pre>  ordered  =3D layers sorted bottom-first (po=
sition, then createdAt)
  refLayer =3D layers[ref.layerId]
  above    =3D the layer immediately above refLayer in `ordered`

  if above exists and above.name =3D=3D 'Draft'  =E2=86=92 reuse: layer =3D=
 { id: above.id }
  else                                       =E2=86=92 create: layer =3D { =
name: 'Draft', abovePosition: refLayer.position }
</pre></div>

<p>So repeated vectorizations of the same image accumulate on one Draft lay=
er, each as its own group, while an image on a different layer (or a Draft =
layer that has since been moved) gets a fresh one. Only the layer <strong>d=
irectly</strong> above is considered; a =E2=80=9CDraft=E2=80=9D two layers =
up is not reused. If the reference=E2=80=99s layer cannot be found, <code>f=
indIndex</code> returns -1, so <code>above</code> is the bottom layer: it i=
s reused if it happens to be named =E2=80=9CDraft=E2=80=9D, otherwise a new=
 layer is created at the bottom (<code>abovePosition</code> -1).</p>
<p>These reads use state captured before the network round trip. <code>vect=
orizeNode</code> takes <code>store =3D useCanvas.getState()</code> once, be=
fore any <code>await</code>, and after the reply reads the board background=
, the layer table and the <code>ref</code> node from that snapshot, while <=
code>insertMany</code> itself runs against fresh state. If the user moves o=
r resizes the reference, or reorders layers, during the call (which can tak=
e tens of seconds), the draft is placed against the old rectangle and the D=
raft-layer decision uses the old layer positions.</p>
