<p>Consequences worth knowing:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>One =E2=8C=98Z</strong> removes every draft node and edge <em>a=
nd</em> the Draft layer if it was created in this call (the layer lives in =
the same snapshot). Undo also clears the selection, and because the current=
 layer (Draft) no longer exists, the current layer falls to the bottom of t=
he stack, typically =E2=80=9CReference=E2=80=9D, not the layer the user was=
 on before. Redo restores nodes, edges and layer with the same ids, but not=
 the selection.</li>
<li>The group means a click on any draft element selects the whole draft (<=
code>expandSelectionToGroups</code>), so the user can nudge or scale the wh=
ole thing against the reference, then =E2=8C=98=E2=87=A7G (Ungroup) to edit=
 pieces.</li>
<li>The canvas paints layers bottom-first and, within a layer, by <code>zIn=
dex</code>. Draft nodes get <code>zIndex</code> values above every existing=
 node, which orders them among themselves in model order; anything added la=
ter, on any layer, gets a higher <code>zIndex</code> still. Their position =
relative to the reference comes from Draft sitting above the reference=E2=
=80=99s layer, not from <code>zIndex</code>.</li>
<li>Edges are on the Draft layer too, so hiding Draft hides its connectors.=
</li>
</ul>
<h3 id=3D"d3-persistence">D.3 Persistence<a class=3D"headerlink" href=3D"fi=
le:///private/var/folders/hj/hx1hqg8908nf89fbssd6mq5h0000gv/T/92.html#d3-pe=
rsistence" title=3D"Permanent link">=EE=A0=86</a></h3>
<p><code>insertMany</code> only marks rows dirty. <code>BoardEditor</code> =
subscribes to the store and, 300 ms after the last change to nodes, edges, =
layers, viewport or current layer, runs <code>flushSave</code> (also on =E2=
=8C=98S and on unmount). <code>flushSave</code> calls <code>consumeDirty()<=
/code> and issues <code>layers.upsertMany</code> first (so every <code>laye=
r_id</code> resolves), then <code>nodes.upsertMany</code> and <code>edges.u=
psertMany</code>, then the viewport and the current layer; main writes them=
 to SQLite. The unmount path issues the same upserts without awaiting them.=
 The draft therefore appears in the <code>.haldraw</code> export and surviv=
es restart like anything else; there is no separate =E2=80=9Cvectorize resu=
lt=E2=80=9D table or file.</p>
<h3 id=3D"d4-how-the-rows-render">D.4 How the rows render<a class=3D"header=
link" href=3D"file:///private/var/folders/hj/hx1hqg8908nf89fbssd6mq5h0000gv=
/T/92.html#d4-how-the-rows-render" title=3D"Permanent link">=EE=A0=86</a></=
h3>
<p>Nothing in the renderer knows a node came from Vectorize. The rows are d=
rawn by the same code as hand-made ones:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Shapes</strong> =E2=80=94 <code>Shape.tsx</code> draws the rect=
/ellipse/diamond with <code>style.fill</code>, <code>style.stroke</code>, <=
code>strokeWidth 2</code>, <code>strokeDasharray</code> if set, <code>corne=
rRadius 8</code> on rects. The label is a <code>foreignObject</code> spanni=
ng the node with a flex <code>div</code>: <code>p-2</code> (8 px padding), =
<code>fontSize</code> from C.5, <code>lineHeight 1.3</code>, <code>whiteSpa=
ce: pre-wrap</code>, <code>wordBreak: break-word</code>, <code>overflow: hi=
dden</code>, alignment from <code>textAlign</code>/<code>verticalAlign</cod=
e> (centre/middle for shapes, left/top for free text). Text that does not f=
it is clipped, not shrunk.</li>
<li><strong>Connectors</strong> =E2=80=94 <code>routing.ts</code> <code>edg=
eEndpoints</code> resolves each end: with <code>anchor 'auto'</code> and a =
target point (the other node=E2=80=99s centre), it compares <code>|dx| =C3=
=97 height</code> against <code>|dy| =C3=97 width</code>; if the horizontal=
 term wins it attaches to the left or right side=E2=80=99s midpoint, else t=
op or bottom. <code>buildPath</code> for <code>'straight'</code> emits <cod=
e>M from L to</code>. <code>Edge.tsx</code> draws that path in the edge=E2=
=80=99s stroke/width/dash, adds the <code>arrow</code> marker at the <code>=
to</code> end via <code>markerEnd</code>, and if a <code>label</code> exist=
s, a 120 =C3=97 24 <code>foreignObject</code> pill at the path midpoint.</l=
i>
<li><strong>Auto-anchor rule, geometrically:</strong> the chosen side is th=
e one the ray from this box=E2=80=99s centre to the other box=E2=80=99s cen=
tre would exit through, using the box=E2=80=99s aspect ratio. For two boxes=
 side by side that is right=E2=86=92left; for stacked boxes it is bottom=E2=
=86=92top; for a diagonal pair it depends on the slope versus the aspect ra=
tio.</li>
</ul>
<div class=3D"highlight"><pre>   |dx|=C2=B7h &gt; |dy|=C2=B7w  =E2=86=92  l=
eft/right side          otherwise  =E2=86=92  top/bottom side
   =E2=94=8C=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=
=E2=94=80=E2=94=90                                    =E2=94=8C=E2=94=80=E2=
=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=90
   =E2=94=82   c =E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=BC=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=
=96=B6 target                          =E2=94=82   c    =E2=94=82
   =E2=94=94=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=
=E2=94=80=E2=94=98                                    =E2=94=94=E2=94=80=E2=
=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=AC=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=80=E2=94=98
                                                     =E2=96=BC target
</pre></div>

<p>Because the edge is attached by node id, moving a draft box later drags =
its connectors with it. That is the payoff for asking the model for endpoin=
ts rather than paths.</p>
